  "notes": {
    "answers": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "text": "Proposed answers to the open questions (7)\n\n1 · Icon granularity: four tray icons — Up to date, Working, Offline, Needs attention. Saved locally / Shared as draft / Finishing up share the Working icon: they last seconds to minutes and the user never acts on them. The window and tooltip name the exact stage.\n\n2 · Paused: reserve the glyph now (two bars badge, shown on the icon sheet as RESERVED) so the set stays coherent, but don't ship it until pause semantics extend ADR-0010.\n\n3 · Quit with an open session: recommend Variant A — no prompt. Quit never loses work, so a modal adds friction for nothing. The menu shows Finish session right above Quit, and Quit carries a one-line hint. Variant B (prompt) is mocked for comparison.\n\n4 · Workspaces per window: one window, several workspaces. A switcher in the title row; with one workspace it reads as a plain name. The tray shows the highest-precedence state across all workspaces.\n\n5 · Attention reason in the 0.3 shell: yes. It's the only thing that turns 'Needs attention' into a next step.\n\n6 · Notifications: only on transitions into or out of Needs attention, and on each new conflict. Same reason never repeats within 30 min; offline never toasts.",
      "w": 520,
      "x": -620,
      "y": 0
    },
